    "body": "**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**\r\nTo comply to the GDPR regulation about:\r\nRight of withdrawal ('the right to be forgotten'): request its deletion when the data is no longer necessary.\r\n\r\nWe need to manage that data without delete user, to avoid possible problematic records about mandatory relationships, airline stats, etc.\r\nI am not sure if this already works like this. In any case, it could be useful if a pilot wants to go back and recover all his progress after asking for his data to be deleted.\r\n\r\nCurrently when we change the user's state to \"deleted\" both their name and email remain in the system.\r\n\r\n**Describe the solution you'd like**\r\nBy changing the state of the pilot to \"deleted\" the system could overwrite his name in the database to something like john doe, or take just the first letters, his initials, \"JDD\" (John Doe Doe) of his full name.\r\nFor email I don't know what would be the perfect solution. ¿And password?\r\n\r\n**Describe alternatives you've considered**\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\n![imagen](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/16170732/197788340-7d3ec21d-4c1e-4578-a0ff-c5700b36b950.png)\r\n",
